      "created_at": "2025-08-03T07:09:36.939Z",
      "cooked": "<p>a wrong exchange rate (14,500 SYP/USD) was used when submitting a Purchase Receipt, which caused an incorrect stock valuation. Later, the correct exchange rate (10,500 SYP/USD) was entered in the Purchase Invoice, but it did not affect the item valuation. Since the Purchase Receipt cannot be cancelled (items from the same batch were already used in subsequent transactions), how can I correctly adjust the stock valuation or account for this currency error retrospectively?</p>\n<p>any one can help please</p>",
